"SAK: Sparse Arguments of Knowledge, from Sparse Lookup Arguments (https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/2143)\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/2143\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 75\nL0: # What a lovely hat\nL1: #### Is it made out of 【0†tin foil†iacr.org】?\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Cryptology ePrint Archive】\nL4: \nL5:   * 【2†Papers】 Updates from the last:\nL6:     * 【3†7 days】\nL7:     * 【4†31 days】\nL8:     * 【5†6 months】\nL9:     * 【6†365 days】\nL10:     * * * *\nL11: \nL12:     * 【7†Listing by year】\nL13:     * 【8†All papers】\nL14:     * 【9†Compact view】\nL15:     * 【10†Subscribe†www.iacr.org】\nL16:     * * * *\nL17: \nL18:     * 【11†How to cite】\nL19:     * * * *\nL20:     * 【12†Harvesting metadata】\nL21:   * 【2†Submissions】\nL22:     * 【13†Submit a paper】\nL23:     * 【14†Revise or withdraw a paper】\nL24:     * 【15†Acceptance and publishing conditions】\nL25: \nL26: 【16†Image: Search Button】\nL27: \nL28: [Input] [Button: Search ]\nL29: #### Paper 2026/2143\nL30: \nL31: ### 【17†SAK: Sparse Arguments of Knowledge, from Sparse Lookup Arguments】\nL32: \nL33: Abhiram Kothapalli, Microsoft Research\nL34: \nL35: Sriram Sridhar, University of California, Berkeley\nL36: \nL37: Arantxa Zapico, Field Extension Institute\nL38: ##### Abstract\nL39: We formalize and construct $sparse$ arguments of knowledge, where given a length $N$ witness that contains $n$ non-zero values the prover time is $O(n) \\circ o(N)$. In particular, we achieve a sparse argument of knowledge for the customizable constraint system relation, which generalizes circuit-satisfiability.\nL40: We achieve this by first utilizing $sublinear$ lookup arguments to provably select only the subset of the constraint system that touches the non-zero entries of the variable assignment, and then running a standard argument of knowledge with mild qualifications. Our resulting sparse argument of knowledge is publicly verifiable and supports a universal and updatable setup.\nL41: It features an $O(N \\log N)$ preprocessing phase, an $O(n \\log n)$ prover time, and an $O(1)$ verifier time, improving on the prior $O(n \\log^2 n)$ and $O(n \\log N)$ prover time.\nL42: ##### Metadata\nL43: \nL44: Available format(s)\nL45:     【17†PDF】\nL46: Category\nL47:     【18†Public-key cryptography】\nL48: Publication info\nL49:     Preprint.\nL50: Keywords\nL51:     【19†Sparse SNARKs】\nL52: Contact author(s)\nL53:     akothapalli @ microsoft com\nL54: srirams @ berkeley edu\nL55: zapico arantxa @ gmail com\nL56: History\nL57:     2026-09-22: approved\nL58:     2026-09-21: received\nL59:     【20†See all versions】\nL60: Short URL\nL61:     【21†https://ia.cr/2026/2143†ia.cr】\nL62: License\nL63: \nL64: 【22†CC BY†creativecommons.org】\nL65: BibTeX 【23†Image】Copy to clipboard\nL66: \nL67:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2026/2143,\nL68:           author = {Abhiram Kothapalli and Sriram Sridhar and Arantxa Zapico},\nL69:           title = {{SAK}: Sparse Arguments of Knowledge, from Sparse Lookup Arguments},\nL70:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2026/2143},\nL71:           year = {2026},\nL72:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/2143}\nL73:     }\nL74: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/pscamillo/icicle-blackwell-ntt/blob/main/REPORT.md\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/pscamillo/icicle-blackwell-ntt/blob/main/REPORT.md: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/pscamillo/icicle-blackwell-ntt/blob/main/LICENSE\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.co