87:   * Object-Oriented Field API: Complete redesign of field operations from static methods to instance methods\nL188:   * Method Chaining Support: Write more concise and expressive code with method chaining\nL189:   * Improved Rust API: Better trait design with standard operator overloading\nL190:   * Enhanced Program API: Reorganized Program module with better type safety\nL191:   * Backward Compatibility: Comprehensive migration guides for v3 to v4 transition\nL192:   * Post Quantum: Implemented a NIST FIPS203 (ML-KEM) protocol on CUDA, fully open-source\nL193:   * Lattice Based Cryptography: Add support for Lattice based cryptography, with integer ring support and a full LaBRADOR prover (soon announced)\nL194: ## 🔄 Breaking Changes\nL195: \nL196: ### C++ API Changes\nL197: \nL198: #### Field Arithmetic Operations\nL199: \nL200: All field operations have been converted from static methods to instance methods\nL201: Check the 【87†migration page†dev.ingonyama.com】 for more details\nL202: \nL203: ### Rust API Changes\nL204: \nL205: #### Arithmetic Trait Redesign\nL206: \nL207: The `FieldImpl` trait has been deprecated and split into focused, orthogonal traits\nL208: ## What's Changed\nL209:   * Negacyclic NTT for polynomial rings by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【89†#930】\nL210:   * Update README.md by 【90†@Shalmoni】 in 【91†#931】\nL211:   * Fixed devdocs link licensing by 【90†@Shalmoni】 in 【92†#933】\nL212:   * Fix collab instructions for version mismatch error by 【93†@jeremyfelder】 in 【94†#935】\nL213:   * Feat: generate JL-projection matrix rows by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【95†#936】\nL214:   * Curve Montgomery Conversion Fix for Host Memory by 【96†@emirsoyturk】 in 【97†#938】\nL215:   * [FIX] Invalid memory access causes hang by 【93†@jeremyfelder】 in 【98†#939】\nL216:   * PQC ML-KEM by 【99†@nonam3e】 and 【100†@dorshmil】 in 【101†#932】\nL217:   * Add PQC documentation to 3.9.0 by 【102†@LeonHibnik】 in 【103†#940】\nL218:   * Changed broken link on readme by 【90†@Shalmoni】 in 【104†#942】\nL219:   * [FEAT] Rust Polynomial-Ring trait and NegacyclicNTT by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【105†#943】\nL220:   * [FEAT] Decompose Polynomial-rings by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【106†#945】\nL221:   * [FEAT] JL-projection Rust wrapper by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【107†#949】\nL222:   * [FEAT] MatMul API by 【108†@lnm-at-work】 in 【109†#871】\nL223:   * [FEAT] Expose Sumcheck protocol challenge vector by 【102†@LeonHibnik】 in 【110†#946】\nL224:   * Timur/pqc go wrappers by 【99†@nonam3e】 in 【111†#944】\nL225:   * [FEAT] Add flattening utilities for polynomial slices into scalar slices by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【112†#952】\nL226:   * [CI] Separate testing by feature by 【93†@jeremyfelder】 in 【113†#913】\nL227:   * [FEAT] Add reinterpretation utilities and polynomial vector operations by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【114†#954】\nL228:   * [FIX] typo in ci.yml by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【115†#959】\nL229:   * [REFACTOR] move matrix transpose to matrix_ops, add PolyRing support and tests by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【116†#961】\nL230:   * [CI] Fix Go tests and Rust bn254 by 【93†@jeremyfelder】 in 【117†#960】\nL231:   * [CI] Move merkle test to hash crate by 【93†@jeremyfelder】 in 【118†#963】\nL232:   * Determine the scalar size according to configuration if provided by 【119†@mickeyasa】 in 【120†#955】\nL233:   * [FEATURE] Pseudorandom field element sampling from seed by 【121†@ChickenLover】 in 【122†#950】\nL234:   * Validate JL projection consistency across backends by 【100†@dorshmil】 in 【123†#956】\nL235:   * devdocs: June 15 Update by 【90†@Shalmoni】 in 【124†#947】\nL236:   * consistent norm check by 【96†@emirsoyturk】 in 【125†#967】\nL237:   * Devdocs quick fix by 【90†@Shalmoni】 in 【126†#969】\nL238:   * [FIX] fix int devision bug in MSM by 【127†@idanfr-ingo】 in 【128†#970】\nL239:   * [Feat] matrix ops rust by 【108†@lnm-at-work】 in 【129†#957】\nL240:   * [FIX] Matmul rust wrappers identify device memory and assert sizes by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【130†#977】\nL241:   * [FIX] Unify Zq and Rq Balanced Base-b Decomposition Using Digit-Major Layout by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【131†#979】